# ==============================================================================
# Sweet Cravings Homemade Desserts — Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. DATABASE CONFIGURATION
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two modes, picked automatically:
# - Empty (below): the app uses its built-in SQLite file
#   (data/sweetcravings.db) with zero setup. This is local development.
# - TURSO_DATABASE_URL set: the app talks to a Turso cloud database
#   instead, through the same code (src/lib/db.ts). This is the live
#   site on Cloudflare Workers, which has no disk that keeps files.
#   The token is needed for a remote database; a local `file:` URL
#   (used by tests) needs no token. See DEPLOY.md for the setup steps.
#   Free plan, checked Nov 2026: 100 databases, 5 GB storage,
#   500M rows read / 10M rows written a month, no card. A free
#   database is archived after 10 days with no activity — any visit
#   to the live site counts as activity, and an archived database
#   can be unarchived with `turso group unarchive <group-name>`.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPERATOR ADMIN SECURITY
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password for the sister / kitchen operator to access /admin.
# - Set a long random password here (or in your hosting provider's env vars).
# - NEVER commit a real password to git, and never share it in chat or docs.
# - If this is empty or missing, admin login is disabled (fails closed).
# - Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 24
#
# HOW TO WRITE IT (this matters — the wrong form silently changes it):
# - ALWAYS wrap the value in SINGLE quotes:
#     ADMIN_PASSWORD='your-password-here'
# - Without quotes, a # in the password cuts the value off at that point,
#   so the password the server checks is shorter than the one you typed
#   and login always fails.
# - NEVER use $ in the password. It is expanded as a variable reference
#   even inside quotes, so the stored value is not what you typed.
# - After creating or changing this file, RESTART the dev server
#   (Ctrl+C, then npm run dev). Passwords are only read when the server
#   starts, so edits made while it runs have no effect until restart.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. INSTANT TELEGRAM KITCHEN ALERTS (100% Free)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a free bot via @BotFather on Telegram, paste credentials here or enter
# them through the Admin Settings dashboard (/admin/settings)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. APP BASE URL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The public address of the site, used for link previews (metadata).
# Locally this is http://localhost:3000. For the live site, set it to
# the Cloudflare address (e.g. https://sweet-cravings.<you>.workers.dev,
# or the real domain once it is pointed at the Worker) — and set it
# BEFORE running the deploy command, because this value is baked into
# the site when it is built. If it is left as the localhost value, the
# shop still works, but shared links preview the wrong address.
# In the Cloudflare dashboard, set this same value as a variable too
# (see DEPLOY.md step 4) so the deployed Worker agrees with the build.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
